The order of the melting points is: C &gt; B &gt; A The resonance structure of amide shows a partial negative charge on oxygen and a partial positive charge on nitrogen. Primary and secondary amides also participate in strong hydrogen bonding, but not tertiary amide.

Propionamide, m.p. = 79 °C; N-methylacetamide, m.p. = 28 °C;

N,N-dimethylformamide, m.p. = -61 °C.
